Anonymous <anonymous@user.com> wrote in <3A3FFCFC.1771BF4B@user.com>:

>How do you set console to serial?

At the SRM prompt, you type
    	set console serial
If you would like to see your choices, type
    	set console
or
    	set console [some invalid option, such as "junk"]

Note:
Since you are unable to type on the local keyboard, you will have to use 
the prompt that is on your first serial port.  If you've got a dumb 
terminal, hook it up.  If you've got a laptop (or another computer) you'll 
have to use a cross-over cable connected to the serial port.  You can use 
pretty much any terminal emulator, including hyperterm.  Your settings 
(almost certainly) should be 9600-8-n-1.  If you're connected but don't see 
anything on your screen, just press enter.  If you are indeed connected, 
the prompt will appear after pressing enter.


