The problem you have is the 433a initially could ship with only an adaptec
SCSI controller, which is only supported by Alphabios and not SRM which is
why you get that error message.

The Adaptec was removed as the primary SCSI controller and replaced by a
Qlogic 1040b. The Adaptec could still be ordered, but as an "additional"
SCSI controller.

The difference between the "a" and the "au" were the options that could be
installed, the "a" had options available that were only supported by NT,
"au" contained only options common to VMS,UNIX and NT.   Firmware is the
same.

oh-ya: with the exception of the units that shipped in dec 97 jan-feb 98,
but they can be reloaded with the new firmware. this was because vms/unix
was not offered initially on the box.

