A little bit of history: Qlogic-1040 used to be the only SCSI controller,
officially supported for Tru64, which you can buy new. Some older cards
were still supported, too - but not sold anymore. In particular, Tru64,
up to, and including version 5.0, supported none of recent Adaptec PCI 
SCSI cards. As a consequence, support for these cards was not in SRM.

However, the most recent version of Tru64 (5.1A, I believe), introduced
support of 2940 - so it, presumably, got included into SRM as well. If
5.1A is supported on your system, then there should be a corresponding
SRM image, which incorporates 2940 support, on the firmware download site.

Regards,

/Serge.P

