I just refreshed my memory.. did a firmware update from floppy on a pws500au
in the lab......

you can do it from srm without forcing the change to alphabios....(so you do
not have to switch back later..)

Download the firmare update image from :

http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/readmes/digitalpw.html#method_
AlphaBIOS

save the image to a fat formatted floppy as "fwupdate.exe"

place the floppy in the Alpha system (PWSXXXa or au)
At the srm prompt type "arc" followed by a CR

>>>arc

The system will invoke the ALPHABios firmware.
While the system is performing selftest, type the F2 key to invoke "setup"
You should see a message on the bottom of the screen stating setup will be
entered when selftest completes.

Select the menu entry "Update ALPHABIOS"
It will read the floppy and restart the system. A menu will be displayed,
select update everything (all ROMS),  then follow the instructions..
finishing with a power cycle

The system will retart to the srm console if thats where you started from
using the arc command. else if you were in the alphabios console  goto setup
again,   cmos setup, advanced setup(F6), select SRM unix console, F10 follow
instructions/ power cycle.

JJ

