We have a dozen 500au's, all equipped with an IDE Toshiba CDROM, which
is recognised by both SRM and Tru64 (versions 5.0, 5.0a and also DEC
Unix 4.0e). SRM loads a sort of SCSI emulation layer for the IDE CD, I
think.

Not that I think this is a good configuration (using the CD for tivial
tasks like installing Applixware from CD brings the system load up to
95%!), I would prefer a SCSI CD in all cases - but IDE CD's seem to
work. And for purposes of installation only, they are sufficient of
course.

Kind Regards,
Tobias.


