ARC was first, then was replaced by ALPHABios.   The reason for their
existence was usoft would not allow non-Intel machines to boot NT directly
from their native consoles. They had to look Intel PC like..... The internal
structures allowed AlphaBios to use driver code from NT to access devices
for boot/display..

SRM = System Reference Manual  named after the document that detailed
VAX/ALPHA console behavior.

ALPHABios is being phased out, ARC is only on older boxes..  The last
firmware release has two version of consoles for the current boxes
(ds10,20,es40) one which has Alphabios and othe other with it removed, the
freed space was used to add Adaptec disk controller to the supported SRM
boot devices on some models.

set os_type nt   + CR +power cycle will restart in AlphaBIOS on psw's  AS
800, 1200,4x00 and their white box variants

set os_type nt + CR + power cycle on 2x00, 1000x, AlphaStation X00 will
restart in ARC console.

JJ


