Thomas Kovacs (Thomas.Kovacs@t-online.de) wrote:

: just installed SuSE 7.0 on my AS2100. worked fine but X will not work. The
: graficcard worked fine under NT 4.0!
....
: (**) SVGA: Using 8 bits per color component
               ^^^^^^
Don't!  Many current graphics cards will not work too well in such
low bit depth - especially on Alpha.  16 is much better value although
I have seen cards which were really happy only in 32 bits (this will
be 24 bits with XFree 4.x and is really the same).
"DefaultColorDepth 16" in your XF86Config will make that a default
even if you run xdm or similar.

  Michal


