That's odd. Is manufacturer Digital Semiconductor? If someone else
then my advice my be incorrect.

> What I surely know is the following:

> * AlphaPC164

That's it, its AlphaPC164. NOT AlphaPC164SX nor AlphaPC164LX.

> * CPU Alpha 21164 500 MHz
> * All SIMMs must be 36-bit and have 70ns or faster access time
> * All SIMMs must be of equal size

And that's very good description of the memory (SX and LX use SDRAM), only
number SIMMs missing. You can use bank of 4 SIMMs (128 bit wide) or bank
of 8 SIMMs (256 bit wide) (there's jumper to choose).
If you now have 8 SIMMs, you can change jumper to 128-bit mode and test
only first bank of 4 SIMMs.

> I think it's a Alpha 21164 SX but I'm not sure about it.

No, and 21164 is not right name for the motherboard. 21164 is processor.
Full name is AlphaPC 164, shortened PC164. SX and LX are called PC164SX,
164SX,SX164,164LX,LX164 etc. full names AlphaPC 164SX and AlphaPC 164LX. 

Some links, where you may find more info:
http://www.alphalinux.org/faq/FAQ.html
http://talisman.alphalinux.org/ALOHcl/
http://www.redhat.com/support/hardware/alpha/6.0/sys.html

/O.K.


