How 'bout this:
You said you want to replace your memory.
You said you need SIMMs, 36-bit, 70ns or faster
What choices do you have left?  Go buy yourself some SIMMs.

Really, you already know everything you need.  If somehow I'm wrong (which 
I don't think I am) rest assured that somebody out there will shoot down 
this message real fast.  We're all pretty good about knocking down ignorant 
messages.

I guess you're probably familiar with memory, but here's some generic info 
just incase you need it:
With 72-pin simms, the following things are true:
- 36-bit means the same as parity.  32-bit means non-parity, and could be 
one of several types (fpm, edo, etc)
- Except for speed, your only choices are usually FPM vs EDO vs Parity.
- The speed 60ns, 70ns, 80ns, etc is a delay time.  So the lower the 
number, the faster.


