Let's see, you want to reinstall the system but are afraid of what can
happen during the installation?

I believe the first thing you need to know is:  Does my Alpha boot up
using AlphaBIOS(graphical menus) or SRM(blue prompt)?  If it's
AlphaBIOS you will then need a DOS labeled disk.  If it's SRM then
you'll need a BSD labeled disk.  Fdisk might give you what appears to
be a problem by not starting the cylinder number on the correct number
(+1 of the previous partition border) but that can be fixed manually.
If you are going to do a fresh install you shouldn't worry about
anything, the worst that can happen will be a perfect install that
won't boot (which can also be fixed manually).

