Hi,

> just installed SuSE 7.0 on my AS2100. worked fine but X will not work. The
> graficcard worked fine under NT 4.0!

Congrats ;)

> Please help me!

Read, understand, help yourself ;-) The Xserver does not detect the
size of the memory on your grafics-board. I highlighted the details
in your excerpt of the Xserver-log.
Solution: Set the memory-size in the Device-section in your config-file.
This is normally /etc/X11/XF86Config
You should have something like this in this file:

Section "Device"
	Identifier	"MyMatroxCard"
	VendorName	"Matrox"
	BoardName       "whatever"
+++     VideoRam	4096
EndSection

The line beginning with "+++" is the one you should add. The value "4096"
is to be replaced with the amount of video-memory, your gfx-board has
( in kBytes ).


> Thanks in advance

Your welcome. In case, you have further trouble, feel free to post ;)

