With the hobbyist program a significant amount of "small end" and personal
interest has been rekindled in OpenVMS (the Open is silent).  And it is
probably the best supported OS on most Alpha platforms unless you want to
play high end graphics or cheap pc-grade third-party SCSI devices (or
otherwise unsupported SCSI devices).  Its a great OS for many uses, and
is getting a lot more support for internet-related apps.

Compaq is doing better by VMS than Digital did under GQ Bob Palmer,
whose life ambition seemed to be to kill VMS and ruin Digital (so 
speaketh a stockholder!) but still niche-marketing it to very high-
end high reliability high availability (read expensive) sites and
limiting support at the middle and low end (though the low end boxes
are still great VMS systems).

If you get two systems, get the hobbyist licenses and media, and build
a cluster you have a truly amazing environment with a fully distributed 
lock manager and facilities that other OS's still can't match.

Worth exploring.

