<zapantis@uvic.ca> wrote in <90ojbt$ru0$1@casper.UVic.CA>:

>I would like to setup KDM on a RH 7.0 alpha, to broadcast XDMCP to our
>Xterms.
>I have been able to configure XDM and GDM, and they both work just fine,
>but I have yet to figure out what is it that I need to do for KDM to
>manage remote X-terms. The online KDM.HTML manual provides no help as it
>only deals with look and feel on local system.
>

Lessee...
In SuSE 6.4 and 7.0, this is what you have to do (should be very similar 
with RH):

edit the file /etc/X11/xdm/xdm-config
Comment out the last line
! DisplayManager.requestPort:   0
...
The Xaccess file must have a * in it, or some other access that allows your 
workstations to connect.  This is default for SuSE, and maybe RH too.

edit /etc/rc.config  ...  (This is SuSE)
Change the line
DISPLAYMANAGER="kdm"

That's it!  In fact, you don't even have to do the second part, it's just 
nice.
The last thing is:
init 3 (for SuSE)
init 5 (for RH)
Test it out.  If all works like you want it to, 
edit /etc/inittab
and change the init default.  (To 3 for SuSE, 5 for RH)

Just thought of one more thing...
If you're already in runlevel 5 (RH) then the command init 5 won't do 
anything.  It might work as is, or you might have to restart the X server.  
Easiest way (not the best way) is:
init 3  (shut down the X environment)
init 5  (start it up again)

Okay, now the REAL LAST thing.
If you don't have any luck with this, ask again.
I've done it before on RH, but I don't have my laptop here.  So I don't 
have the file that I wrote down the details in.  If you ask again, I'll be 
able to give you the right answer.


